                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of America
                            for Sabanilla</hi>.</placeName></p>
                <p>I, the undersigned, consul of the United States of America for Sabanilla, do
                    hereby certify that the foregoing signatures are those of Juan de la C. Ruiz,
                    governor of the province, and Gregorio J. Aragon, government secretary; that
                    they are the same as they are accustomed to use in all their official acts, and
                    as such are worthy of full faith and credit.</p>
                <p>Given under my hand and the seal of this consulate at the city of Barranquilla,
                    this — day of December, A. D. 1865.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">W. A. CHAPMAN, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul</hi>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
